# EXPECT-VIOLATION: mirash:InstanceOfDirectionShape
#
# An installed drive is declared instance_of its MANUFACTURER. A manufacturer makes models; it is
# not one. Before #5528 this conformed: RDFS inference types the object of instance_of as an asset
# class, and the old rule only asked "is it an asset class?". The rule now also looks at what the
# object was declared as.

@prefix mira: <https://ontology.factorylm.com/mira#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/fx#> .

ex:rockwell a mira:Manufacturer .
ex:vfd_101  a mira:AssetInstance ; mira:instance_of ex:rockwell .
